      "end_mono": 358413.910253208,
      "raw_response": "Claim: Migraine with aura is associated with ischemic stroke.\n\nANSWER: SUPPORTED. The abstract states, \"Studies were heterogeneous for participant characteristics and definition of cardiovascular disease. Nine studies investigated the association between any migraine and ischaemic stroke (pooled relative risk 1.73, 95% confidence interval 1.31 to 2.29). Additional analyses indicated a significantly higher risk among people who had migraine with aura (2.16, 1.53 to 3.03) compared with people who had migraine without aura (1.23, 0.90 to 1.69; meta-regression for aura status P=0.02).\"\n\nSources:\n\n- Oxford Journals (Meta-analysis): http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmedhealth/pmhhome.cgi?term=Migraine+and+cardiovascular+disease",
